  "output": "# 🔒 Security Audit Report: CarabinerOS Frontend\n\nI've performed a comprehensive security analysis of the Next.js frontend codebase. Here are my findings:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"vulnerabilities\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"file\": \"src/hooks/use-workspace.ts\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"description\": \"Parameter Injection / URL Parameter Encoding Vulnerability. The 'locationId' parameter is concatenated directly into the URL string without encoding. Attacker can inject arbitrary query parameters or path traversal sequences. Use URLSearchParams or URL constructor instead.\",\n      \"code\": \"`${endpoint}?location_id=${locationId}`\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-90: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an HTTP Request\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"file\": \"src/lib/csrf.ts\",\n      \"line\": 16,\n      \"description\": \"CSRF Token Cookie Missing Security Flags. Cookie set without 'HttpOnly' or 'Secure' flags. Missing HttpOnly allows XSS attacks to steal the token via JavaScript. Missing Secure flag allows MITM attacks on HTTP connections.\",\n      \"code\": \"document.cookie = `csrf_token_${runtimeId}=${csrfToken}; SameSite=Strict; Path=/`;\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-614: Sensitive Cookie in HTTPS Session Without Secure Attribute\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/lib/socket-client.ts\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"description\": \"Missing Socket.IO Origin Validation. No explicit origin validation configured for Socket.IO connection. While 'withCredentials' is set, lack of origin check allows potential CSRF attacks from malicious websites.\",\n      \"code\": \"stateSyncSocket = io(`${A0_SOCKET_URL}/state_sync`, { ... });\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/hooks/use-action-cards.ts\",\n      \"line\": 30,\n      \"description\": \"Unvalidated Data from Backend (XSS Risk). Data from agent response (kvps.item, log.content) is stored without validation and will be rendered in the UI. If backend is compromised or returns malicious content, could lead to XSS.\",\n      \"code\": \"item: kvps.item as Record<string, unknown> | undefined, summary: log.content.slice(0, 120)\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/hooks/use-chat.ts\",\n      \"line\": 74,\n      \"description\": \"No Input Validation on User Messages. User text is sent directly to backend without client-side validation. While backend should validate, missing client-side checks for length, encoding, or content type allow potential DoS or injection attacks.\",\n      \"code\": \"body: JSON.stringify({ text, context: contextIdRef.current || '', })\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-20: Improper Input Validation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"next.config.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"description\": \"Unvalidated Environment Variable Fallback. A0_URL defaults to localhost without validation. In edge cases, invalid URLs could cause issues. Should validate URL format.\",\n      \"code\": \"const A0_URL = process.env.A0_URL || 'http://localhost:5000';\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-95: Improper Neutralization of Directives in Dynamically Evaluated Code\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"src/lib/socket-client.ts\",\n      \"line\": 14,\n      \"description\": \"Client-side Socket URL Configuration. NEXT_PUBLIC_A0_URL is client-accessible. While not a direct vulnerability, hardcoding socket URLs in client code reduces flexibility. Should consider reverse proxy in production.\",\n      \"code\": \"const A0_SOCKET_URL = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_A0_URL || '';\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"riskScore\": 72,\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"CRITICAL\",\n      \"title\": \"Fix URL Parameter Encoding in useWorkspace\",\n      \"fix\": \"Replace string concatenation with URLSearchParams constructor:\\n```typescript\\nconst url = new URL(endpoint, window.location.origin);\\nif (locationId) url.searchParams.set('location_id', locationId);\\nfetch(url.toString(), { credentials: 'include' })\\n```\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"CRITICAL\",\n      \"title\": \"Add HttpOnly and Secure Flags to CSRF Token Cookie\",\n      \"fix\": \"The cookie should be set by the backend (Agent Zero) with HttpOnly=true, Secure=true flags. If client-side setting is necessary, use a library that handles this. Current approach:\\n```typescript\\n// Backend should set: Set-Cookie: csrf_token_X=value; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict\\n// Remove client-side cookie setting or use httpOnly workaround\\n```\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"title\": \"Add Socket.IO Origin Validation\",\n      \"fix\": \"Configure explicit origin whitelist:\\n```typescript\\nstateSyncSocket = io(`${A0_SOCKET_URL}/state_sync`, {\\n  autoConnect: false,\\n  transports: ['polling', 'websocket'],\\n  withCredentials: true,\\n  allowUpgrade: false,  // Prevent downgrades\\n  secure: true,  // Only https in production\\n  auth: (cb) => { ... }\\n});\\n```\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Input Validation for Chat Messages\",\n      \"fix\": \"Add client-side validation before sending:\\n```typescript\\nfunction validateMessage(text: string): string {\\n  const trimmed = text.trim();\\n  if (trimmed.length === 0) throw new Error('Empty message');\\n  if (trimmed.length > 2000) throw new Error('Message too long');\\n  return trimmed;\\n}\\n```\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"title\": \"Sanitize Rendered Content from Backend\",\n      \"fix\": \"When rendering action cards and chat content, use DOMPurify or sanitize-html:\\n```typescript\\nimport DOMPurify from 'dompurify';\\n// Before rendering: DOMPurify.sanitize(log.content)\\n```\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"title\": \"Validate and Type-Check Backend Data\",\n      \"fix\": \"Create Zod/Yup schemas for all backend responses:\\n```typescript\\nconst ActionCardSchema = z.object({\\n  id: z.string().uuid(),\\n  module: z.string().max(50),\\n  action: z.string().max(100),\\n  item: z.record(z.unknown()).optional(),\\n});\\n```\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"title\": \"Validate Environment Variable Format\",\n      \"fix\": \"Validate A0_URL at build time:\\n```typescript\\nconst url = new URL(process.env.A0_URL || 'http://localhost:5000');\\nif (!['http:', 'https:'].includes(url.protocol)) throw new Error('Invalid A0_URL');\\n```\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"LOW\",\n      \"title\": \"Add CSP (Content Security Policy) Header\",\n      \"fix\": \"In next.config.ts:\\n```typescript\\nasync headers() {\\n  return [{ source: '/(.*)', headers: [\\n    { key: 'Content-Security-Policy', value: \\\"default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self' ws:\\\" }\\n  ]}]\\n}\\n```\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"LOW\",\n      \"title\": \"Review package.json Dependencies\",\n      \"fix\": \"Run: `npm audit` and `pnpm outdated` to check for vulnerable transitive dependencies. Pin versions or use security scanning tools like Snyk.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"checklist\": {\n    \"hardcodedSecrets\": \"✓ No API keys or passwords found in code\",\n    \"sqlInjection\": \"⚠️ Parameter injection risk in use-workspace.ts (not traditional SQL, but URL parameter injection)\",\n    \"xssVulnerabilities\": \"⚠️ Potential XSS from unvalidated backend content in action cards and chat\",\n    \"insecureDependencies\": \"✓ Dependencies look current (check with `npm audit`)\",\n    \"authorizationIssues\": \"⚠️ CSRF token missing HttpOnly flag; Socket.IO lacks origin validation\",\n    \"envLeaks\": \"✓ Proper use of NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix for client-side vars\",\n    \"inputValidation\": \"✗ No visible input validation before sending to backend\",\n    \"outputEncoding\": \"⚠️ No visible sanitization of rendered content\"\n  },\n  \"summary\": \"The frontend has moderate security posture but requires fixes for parameter encoding, CSRF cookie security, and input/output validation. The highest-risk issue is parameter injection in the workspace endpoint. The architecture relies on backend validation, which is fragile if the backend is compromised.\"\n}\n```\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Critical Issues:**\n1. **URL parameter injection** in `use-workspace.ts` — locationId not URL-encoded\n2. **CSRF token cookie** missing HttpOnly/Secure flags — vulnerable to XSS theft\n\n**What's Working Well:**\n- No hardcoded secrets or credentials\n- Proper CSRF token flow established\n- Session cookies + withCredentials enabled\n- Modern dependencies (React 19, Next.js 16)\n- Socket.IO using polling+websocket transport (good for cross-browser)\n\n**Missing Layers:**\n- Input validation (client-side only)\n- Output sanitization (especially for markdown/HTML content)\n- Content Security Policy headers\n- Origin validation for Socket.IO\n\nWould you like me to create fixes for the critical issues, or generate a detailed remediation plan?\n",
